//RS /// Cross-process lock guarding the slow path (rewrite + `cargo build`) of the
//RS /// FFI bridge cache for one cache key. Same atomic `create_dir` + stale-steal
//RS /// shape as `tests/common/mod.rs` `FfiBridgeLock`, kept as a *separate* lock
//RS /// (different failure domain: this one guards real concurrent `jet`
//RS /// processes; the test lock also serializes different test *binaries* in the
//RS /// same suite run) — scoped per cache key rather than global, and
//RS /// error-returning instead of panicking, since this runs in the compiler
//RS /// itself and must never crash a build (I2: no path here may surface as an
//RS /// internal panic in place of a diagnostic).
